  "releaseNotes": "Security fix: sensitive HTTP headers are now redacted in diagnostic output.\n\n      Previously AuthenticatedHttpClientHandler joined every request and response header, key and\n      value, into its Debug level log message. The handler adds DD-API-KEY and DD-APPLICATION-KEY to\n      each request, so both keys were written verbatim. Any consumer running at Debug retained usable\n      credentials for the life of its log store, and neither key expires.\n\n      DD-API-KEY and DD-APPLICATION-KEY are now redacted, along with Authorization,\n      Proxy-Authorization, Cookie, Set-Cookie and common API key header names, case-insensitively, on\n      request and response. The credential length is retained, so requests remain diagnosable without\n      exposing the value. The log line format is otherwise unchanged.\n\n      Consumers should upgrade, review existing Debug logs for previously captured keys, and rotate\n      any key that appears in them.",
